        <type>void</type>
        <definition>static void sigIntHandler</definition>
        <argsstring>(int signum)</argsstring>
        <name>sigIntHandler</name>
        <param>
          <type>int</type>
          <declname>signum</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Signal handler for SIGINT (Ctrl+C). </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This handler is registered via sigaction() to catch the SIGINT signal, which is typically generated when the user presses Ctrl+C in the terminal. Instead of terminating the process immediately, it perform a controlled application exit.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>signum</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Signal number that triggered the handler. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
<para>Unused because we have only registered SIGINT, so the value will always be SIGINT (2), which corresponds to Ctrl+C.</para>
        </inbodydescription>
